  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f636023f-3188-48ba-881d-4f2c9dc3cb77"],
 " are the same with the sphere given as a token."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"d6de12e2-fb1c-43c9-a588-8f08839087ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In the band ",
 StyleBox["B = {v \[NotEqual] c : r \[LessEqual] d(c, v) \[LessEqual] s}", 
  "TI"],
 " a wall is a set ",
 StyleBox["W \[SubsetEqual] B", "TI"],
 " that separates ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " from the vertices beyond ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 ", induces a connected subgraph, and has no proper subset that does both. ",
 StyleBox["W", "TI"],
 " separates when every path from ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " to a vertex ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " with ",
 StyleBox["d(c, v) > s", "TI"],
 " meets ",
 StyleBox["W", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"12c31d62-8669-408c-b678-aace7aa613fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One draw is a greedy search. It starts from a connected piece of ",
 StyleBox["B", "TI"],
 " that separates, chosen at random, and removes one vertex at a time, chosen \
uniformly among the vertices whose removal leaves a connected separating set, \
until no vertex can go. The result is a wall: if a smaller connected \
separating set lay inside, some vertex outside it could still go. The draw is \
fast, and it is not uniform over the walls."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e390cc88-e57b-4a26-93d4-38843bea47f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With a count ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " the draws are distinct: each further draw runs the same search but avoids \
the sets all of whose walls were drawn already. ",
 Cell[BoxData["All"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d8a1171a-24ea-4aa7-ab30-6624481ba6ad"],
 " gives every wall, sorted; that search can take a time exponential in the \
size of the band."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"3e3e0c6e-7af6-4aa0-bd8f-35448d4a4dcb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On the square grid, which is bipartite, a shell of one radius has no edges, \
and a sphere of one radius does not exist; a band {",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " + 1} has walls, closed zigzags between its two shells. When no connected \
part of the band separates, the result is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a372ebaf-efa4-4798-b86d-be609b3cae20"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9b6d9a83-3c9d-4404-92cf-d60dd84ae67d"],

Cell["Options:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"7b452ae1-0b9b-4327-9648-12d7e5ca59d2"],

